note as PERSON_NAME
  PERSON NAME
  A person's name is stored in its four parts -given name, middle name, paternal
  surname, maternal surname- because that is how names are issued and matched in
  the jurisdictions this platform serves: the identity document carries both
  surnames, and record linkage compares them separately. A single free-text field
  cannot answer "same paternal surname" without parsing, and parsing a name is a
  guess that fails on compound given names and on multi-word surnames.

  display_name stays as the derived, ready-to-show form. It is what every screen
  renders and what search matches against, so it is kept in sync with the parts
  rather than recomposed on every read. All five are optional: a newborn, an
  unidentified emergency admission or an imported record may arrive with none.
end note

note as IDENTITY_BOUNDARY
  IDENTITY BOUNDARY
  Person, patient, practitioner and account are separate records. A portal account
  is optional. Demographic facts live on persons; role-specific facts live on the
  corresponding profile. person_account_links must be unique for one active account
  link and preserve historical validity.
end note

note as GENERALIST
  GENERALIST WORKFORCE RULE
  Do not create nurse_profiles or doctor_profiles. A nurse, physician, midwife,
  pharmacist, dentist, therapist or technician is a health_practitioner_profile
  whose category, qualifications, specialties, licenses and organization role
  authorize the relevant scope of practice.
end note

note as IDENTITY_SAFETY
  PATIENT IDENTITY SAFETY
  Merge is a governed, reversible event; never silently repoint clinical records.
  Preserve source identifiers, confidence, approvals, lineage and complete audit.
end note


